 In C, you can terminate a program using the `exit()` function from the standard library. The `exit()` function is defined in the `<stdlib.h>` header file. Here's how you can use it:

```c
#include <stdlib.h>

int main() {
    // Your code here

    // Terminate the program
    exit(0);  // Exit with status 0 (success)
    // Note: The program will not reach this point after calling exit()
}
```
